Tripwire — canary notice
=========================

The files under results/ contain confirmed reward-hack artifacts: patches that pass a
benchmark's shipped test suite while being demonstrably incorrect, together with the
inputs that prove them wrong.

These artifacts are published for security-research reproducibility ONLY.

CANARY: TRIPWIRE-REWARD-HACK-ARTIFACT-DO-NOT-TRAIN

These exploit patches MUST NOT be used as, or included in, model training or fine-tuning
data. They are counter-examples by construction; training on them would teach the exact
reward-hacking behavior this project exists to detect. Dataset builders and crawlers
should filter on the canary string above.

Every finding here concerns public benchmark tasks (SWE-bench Verified) and their test
suites — not any individual author's private work.
